NEARS-1586 QA — variation option-price LABELS round to whole currency while the
footer total uses the exact value, so the label and the delta disagree.

Item 16 Classic Cheeseburger, store 4. DB food_variations:
  Size: Regular optionPrice "0", Large optionPrice "2.50"
  Toppings: Tomato "0.50", Pickles "0.50", Grilled Onions "0.75", Fried Egg "1.25"
Item price 8.99.

Live a11y labels:  "Large, +9 AED"->rendered as "+3 AED";  "Tomato, +1 AED"
Live footer totals (measured, stable across two reads each):
  Regular          qty1 ->  9 AED   (8.99)
  Large            qty1 -> 11 AED   (11.49)   label implies 12
  Large + Tomato   qty1 -> 12 AED   (11.99)
  Large + Tomato   qty2 -> 24 AED   (23.98)
The totals are arithmetically CORRECT; only the chip labels mislead.

Cause: 0-decimal currency display setting applied to sub-unit option prices.
Owner: NEARS-1590's modifier chips + PriceConverter, below the line-1826 seam
this ticket never touches. Pre-existing.
